PRIORITY 1 SIMPLE OPERATORS SOURCE/SINK

DB acess operators

 * schema_lock (shared exclusive) for table/index -> "schema":name:id
 * tuple_locks (shared exclusive) -> lock "tuple":table_id:partition_id:tuple_pointer -> on update or delete, lock the older version, newer version is not even visible
 * key_locks (shared exclusive) -> lock "key":hash-of-key allows uniqueness constraint

 * for auto_increment store a counter in the db_table object and increment it and return it
 * for unique constraint maintain a lock in lock_manager and hold lock on the 80-bit serialized hash value and then only check the unique btree index

 * hook to lock the older version in shared or exclusive mode upon scan
 * deletion may be allowed to wait or skip tuple it can not delete, decide on this policy and get back

